```c
int jpc_dec_process_siz(jpc_dec_t *dec, jpc_ms_t *ms)
{
    jpc_siz_t *siz = &ms->parms.siz;
    // ...
    // Calculate tile dimensions
    dec->xstart = siz->xosiz;
    dec->ystart = siz->yosiz;
    dec->xend = siz->xsiz;
    dec->yend = siz->ysiz;
    dec->tilewidth = siz->xtsiz - siz->xtosiz;
    dec->tileheight = siz->ytsiz - siz->ytosiz;
    dec->numhtiles = JPC_CEILDIV(dec->xend - dec->xtosiz, dec->tilewidth);
    dec->numvtiles = JPC_CEILDIV(dec->yend - dec->ytosiz, dec->tileheight);
    // ...
    // Calculate image size
    // ...
}
```

The issue is likely that JasPer computes the image size as `xsiz - xosiz` which is small (15), but then later uses xsiz itself in a calculation that causes a huge allocation.

